  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nPost 3-axis milling programs for machines running [grblHAL](https://github.com/grblHAL), the open controller firmware used on many hobby and small-shop routers and mills (RP2040/RP2350, STM32, ESP32, Teensy boards). CamCraft has no grbl-family post yet; the closest is `tormach.cps` (LinuxCNC dialect), but grblHAL understands a smaller subset and posting Tormach output to it fails or misbehaves.\n\nI'm building a grblHAL machine and its sender, so I can test the output against a real controller once it runs, and against grblHAL's simulator before that.\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\nA new `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` (3-axis mill), structured like `tormach.cps` and specced from grblHAL's public documentation and the RS-274/LinuxCNC G-code references (behaviour only; no grblHAL source read, as it is GPL), plus a generic `assets/machines/grblhal-3axis.mch`.\n\nWhat the post has to respect (each one to be checked against grblHAL's docs while writing it):\n- **No cutter compensation**: grblHAL has no G41/G42, so the post always takes CamCraft's computed (in-computer) path and refuses an operation set to control compensation, by name.\n- **Tool length**: G43.1 (dynamic tool length offset, Z) by default, with an option for G43 H when the controller has a tool table.\n- **Tool change**: `M6 T<n>` on a line of its own, followed by the length offset on the next line (some senders hold the M6 line and drop the rest of it); Z up first.\n- **Canned cycles**: G81/G82/G83 (and G73) when enabled in the post's options, otherwise expanded into G0/G1 moves.\n- Spindle M3/M4/M5 with S, coolant M7/M8/M9, WCS G54-G59, G90/G94/G17/G21 (or G20), arcs G2/G3 in the XY plane, program end M30, comments in parentheses.\n\n**Done means:** `grblhal.cps` and the machine file ship in `assets/`; the post is in the conformance list and the cross-post tests (`comment_escape`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `comp`) like `tormach`; a `grblhal_post` test and goldens under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/grblhal/` cover contour, pocket, face, slot, trace, drill, peck and tool change; control compensation is refused with a named reason.\n",
